e degree",5]],"inflections":[["undemokratischeren","undemokratisch","comparative,genitive,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"wabbeln":{"entries":[["wabbeln",null,"/ˈvabəln/","From Middle High German wabelen, merged with related Middle Low German *wabbelen. To the former compare Old Norse vafla, to the latter dialectal Dutch wobbelen, English wabble, wobble. All of these are iteratives of Proto-Germanic *wabōną, related to *webaną (“to weave”), whence Middle High German waben (“to move about”), Old English wafian (modern English wave).\nIn the High German form, the -bb- is due to blocking of open-syllable lengthening, which is fairly common before the syllables -el- and -er-. In the Low German form it must be due to expressive gemination.",null,"haben"]],"senses":[[339937,"wabbeln","verb","to wobble, wiggle, jiggle; said of jelly/jello, human body fat, and the like",0,null,["informal"]]]},"batistnes":{"inflections":[["batistnes","batisten","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"beigesellet":{"inflections":[["beigesellet","beigesellen","plural,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-i,subordinate-clause"]]},"bärenfleische":{"inflections":[["bärenfleische","bärenfleisch","dative,singular"]]},"geisterrade":{"inflections":[["geisterrade","geisterrad","dative,singular"]]},"kirchgängern":{"inflections":[["kirchgängern","kirchgänger","dative,definite,plural"]]},"knüppeldämme":{"inflections":[["knüppeldämme","knüppeldamm","plural"]]},"nullmeilensteinen":{"inflections":[["nullmeilensteinen","nullmeilenstein","dative,definite,plural"]]}}}